MODEL_FEEDBACK_JSON:
{
  "positive_alignment_reasons": [
    "The solder-seal connectors fit my previous circuit-board and relay projects because they help join and insulate wiring, giving me a clear reason to use them.",
    "The inspection mirror feels useful for checking hidden wiring and fasteners during repairs. The mounting magnets also connect to my earlier interest in reclosable fasteners, although I would wait for a specific mounting job before choosing them."
  ],
  "negative_misalignment_reasons": [
    "The large heat-shrink tubing and specialized changeover switch relate to electrical work, but their dimensions or intended uses do not clearly fit my small circuit projects.",
    "The polishing wheels and compounds assume a finishing project I have not shown a need for. The exam gloves and rapid test likewise have no immediate purpose for me, and the gloves introduce uncertain sizing and unnecessary quantities."
  ],
  "overgeneralized_signals": [
    "My interest in practical repair supplies seems to have been stretched into an interest in almost any workshop supply, even when it serves a different task.",
    "Electrical wording seems to count too much: a connector for project wiring, a large insulation tube, and a specialized selector switch are not equally useful to me."
  ],
  "missing_or_underweighted_signals": [
    "My breadboards, PCB supplies, battery holder, and relay suggest that compatibility with small electronics matters, including dimensions and a clear role in the wiring.",
    "I choose supplies when I can identify a concrete use. Something potentially useful, like mounting magnets, can interest me without being something I would buy now."
  ],
  "summary_diagnosis": "You recognized my interest in hands-on projects, but often missed the specific task, scale, and immediate need that make a supply worth choosing."
}
